title: '2026-11-12: deep subscription reports, first mission'
pid: 2a2a8671-8183-4b80-b4a8-d2a12f940703
body: |2-
  Done, under "what I know": a map of following as built, the design
  space for reporting at depth (region and baseline, five baselines,
  what I would build), how merging through forks goes today and why it
  is awkward, and eight questions for Jeff, each standalone.
  Where Vic and I meet: the store of "processed" marks with fingerprints
  is one thing for both of us. The view of another's changes is Vic's;
  the region a subscription covers and the count it shows are mine.
  Ed's note on consuming Jeff's changes is evidence for both of us.
  Unsure: I ran nothing. What is drawn where, I read from
  'server/refresh/' ('goal.rs', 'visit.rs', 'viewnodestats.rs'), not
  from a running view.
  Surprised: below the first layer a fork already shows the author's
  changes; what is missing is the notice, not the content. And the
  subscriber's own structure is already its "processed" mark for the
  first layer.
  The reader's journal (baseline 5) would live in the repo watcher and
  the session stores, which suits Jesus (unborn) more than me.
